1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:04,596
Picture this.

2
00:00:04,596 --> 00:00:05,869
You're shopping online

3
00:00:05,869 --> 00:00:10,068
and you find a jacket, a dress, or an abaya you really like.

4
00:00:10,068 --> 00:00:11,823
The photos look great.

5
00:00:11,823 --> 00:00:13,744
But you still have a question.

6
00:00:13,744 --> 00:00:15,498
What would it look like on me?

7
00:00:15,498 --> 00:00:19,423
That's where GRINDCTRL’s AI Virtual Try-On comes in.

8
00:00:22,923 --> 00:00:25,894
Inside a supported Shopify fashion store,

9
00:00:25,894 --> 00:00:27,467
a shopper chooses a product

10
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:29,450
and selects the Try-On option.

11
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:33,761
They upload a photo of themselves, then request a personalized preview.

12
00:00:37,261 --> 00:00:42,157
The system generates an image showing how the selected garment could look
on that person.

13
00:00:42,157 --> 00:00:44,236
It's a visual exploration tool,

14
00:00:44,236 --> 00:00:46,835
not a promise of an exact physical fit.

15
00:00:46,835 --> 00:00:52,063
But it gives shoppers a more personal way to explore clothing than product
photography alone.

16
00:00:55,563 --> 00:00:57,768
Now imagine the next question.

17
00:00:57,768 --> 00:01:00,154
Does this item run true to size?

18
00:01:00,154 --> 00:01:01,636
What are the delivery options?

19
00:01:02,012 --> 00:01:04,047
How should the fabric be cared for?

20
00:01:04,047 --> 00:01:06,583
Instead of searching through multiple pages,

21
00:01:06,583 --> 00:01:09,366
the shopper can open Store Chat and ask.

22
00:01:09,366 --> 00:01:14,081
The assistant uses the information the merchant has provided to answer
relevant questions

23
00:01:14,325 --> 00:01:16,128
in English or Arabic.

24
00:01:16,128 --> 00:01:18,412
If a situation needs human judgment,

25
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:21,175
the conversation can be handed to the store's team.

26
00:01:21,175 --> 00:01:23,042
The team can review the thread,

27
00:01:23,042 --> 00:01:25,069
understand why it was handed over,

28
00:01:25,069 --> 00:01:27,710
and continue the conversation from the shared inbox.

29
00:01:31,662 --> 00:01:32,525
Together,

30
00:01:32,525 --> 00:01:36,827
these two experiences connect two important moments in fashion shopping.

31
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:40,822
Virtual Try-On helps the customer explore a garment visually.

32
00:01:40,822 --> 00:01:45,286
Store Chat helps them understand the product and find the information they
need.

33
00:01:45,286 --> 00:01:50,121
And the human team remains part of the experience when personal support
matters.

34
00:01:50,121 --> 00:01:51,132
For the merchant,

35
00:01:51,132 --> 00:01:55,249
both features are designed around the Shopify store they already operate.

36
00:01:55,249 --> 00:01:58,431
The demonstration lets you explore a real storefront.

37
00:01:58,431 --> 00:01:59,899
Try the product journey

38
00:01:59,899 --> 00:02:02,269
and see how the chat works with store knowledge.

39
00:02:02,697 --> 00:02:05,415
There are no imaginary performance numbers here

40
00:02:05,415 --> 00:02:07,119
and no magic promises.

41
00:02:07,119 --> 00:02:11,756
Just practical tools built to make the online shopping journey more
useful.

42
00:02:15,256 --> 00:02:20,598
See AI Virtual Try-On and Store Chat together at grindctrl.cloud.

43
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:21,868
GRINDCTRL.

44
00:02:21,868 --> 00:02:23,357
Let shoppers see it.

45
00:02:23,357 --> 00:02:24,680
Let them ask.
